# node-waf configurationExcellent, we found the exact issue (and this is fixable)
Great news: the error is clear and specific. Your push is blocked by GitHub Push Protection because firebase-debug.log contains a leaked OAuth token in commit d33a7aa....

🔍 What happened
Remote rejects push:
GH013: Repository rule violations for refs/heads/master
Push cannot contain secrets
Secret location:
firebase-debug.log line ~61
in commit d33a7aa63557b6609512b9f9bfbe45e2fbcdb16d
🛠️ Step-by-step fix
Remove secret from file (and ideally from history):

open firebase-debug.log, remove or redact token line(s)
ideally add to .gitignore (if should never be committed)
Commit change:

git add firebase-debug.log
git commit -m "Remove exposed OAuth token from firebase-debug.log"
Rewrite history to remove secret commits forever

Quick but careful:
git filter-branch --force --index-filter 'git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch firebase-debug.log' --prune-empty --tag-name-filter cat -- --all
or better, use BFG:
bfg --delete-files firebase-debug.log
then:
git push --force origin master
If you must preserve other commits but you can’t rewrite, use GitHub unblock URL (temporary):

the URL in error message: .../security/secret-scanning/unblock-secret/...
but still remove token from repo; don't commit it again.
💡 Additional safe steps
Ensure firebase-debug.log is in .gitignore:
add line: firebase-debug.log
Re-run:
git status
git log --oneline --graph --decorate --firebase-debug.log (check history)
Use git show d33a7aa...:firebase-debug.log to confirm the secret is removed from pointed commit in result.
⚠️ Important security note
Even after removing from git, rotate that exposed OAuth token immediately in Firebase/GitHub/etc.
Treat it as compromised, as leak already triggered rule detection.

🎯 Final push
After clean history + secrets removed:

git push origin master (or --force if history rewritten)
verify no push protection error.
You’re almost done; this is exactly the right case where secret-scan blocks the commit and safe re-write is required.
